eaning electorate with a three-term Democratic incumbent, Darren Soto, making this one of the cycle's most watched House races. Soto has outraised challenger Dan Green and holds a large cash advantage, and he has leaned on union endorsements, Spanish-language advertising, and claims of bipartisan work. Green, a fresh nominee from a crowded primary, has the police union's backing and the wind of a favorable national map at his back.\n\nMost professional raters now call the race a Republican flip opportunity, though a few still rate it a tossup. The single available poll, from August, showed the candidates tied. Markets lean clearly toward Green. The forecast lands as a modest Republican edge, with Soto's incumbency and money keeping him competitive but the district's fundamentals doing most of the work.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.3442, "margin": -2.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2846, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2806, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3778, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2308, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3096, "margin": -2.6}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3559, "margin": -2.6}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3413, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3329, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2822, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.28, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2817, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2782, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2318, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2308, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2625, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3059, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2911, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.2268, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.2279, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0